WEBVTT

NOTE Paragraph boundaries measured from synthesis; timing within paragraphs is approximate.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.214
Attack surface analysis
establishes which assets

00:00:03.214 --> 00:00:07.285
and interfaces may be reachable and
how they relate to the organization.

00:00:07.285 --> 00:00:10.677
Inputs include authorized
discovery results, domain records,

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:15.370
service observations, cloud inventories,
application routes, and ownership records.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.046
A list of addresses is only
a starting point; an assessment needs

00:00:19.046 --> 00:00:23.060
to connect services with their purpose,
exposure, and responsible team.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.040
Models can normalize
inconsistent service descriptions

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.240
and propose links between
overlapping records. A hostname,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.213
a certificate name, and a cloud
endpoint may describe related resources.

00:00:33.213 --> 00:00:37.793
A useful inventory preserves each source
and observation time, records the proposed

00:00:37.793 --> 00:00:41.821
relationship, and separates confirmed
attributes from unresolved matches.

00:00:41.821 --> 00:00:46.180
It should not silently merge records
merely because names resemble one another.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.658
Identity, ownership, and exposure
require different evidence.

00:00:49.658 --> 00:00:53.249
Shared hosting can place unrelated
services behind one address.

00:00:53.249 --> 00:00:57.867
A certificate name does not prove that
the organization owns the current service.

00:00:57.867 --> 00:01:01.972
Confirm ownership against authoritative
records or the responsible team,

00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:05.848
and verify exposure through permitted
network or application checks.

00:01:05.848 --> 00:01:10.580
Document inaccessible and untested areas
instead of calling the inventory complete.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.428
Comparing dated snapshots
can reveal new listeners,

00:01:13.428 --> 00:01:16.612
changed routes, or resources
absent from earlier records.

00:01:16.612 --> 00:01:20.298
AI can summarize those differences
into an attack surface document

00:01:20.298 --> 00:01:23.091
and highlight relationships
needing investigation.

00:01:23.091 --> 00:01:27.000
Analysts then distinguish actual
changes from missing collection data.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.687
The practical deliverable is a
traceable inventory with ownership,

00:01:30.687 --> 00:01:32.586
exposure, and uncertainty visible.

00:01:32.586 --> 00:01:36.719
Automating attack surface documentation
is a natural area for deeper study

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:40.740
because it turns recurring discovery
output into an assessment resource.
